If the opponents come in after the transfer has been completed, responder
doubles with invitational or better values and otherwise passes.

1N-2D-2H-(bid)-
D = 8+ hcp

1N-2H-2S-(bid)-
D = 8+ hcp

After a natural 2NT invitation, an overcall leaves opener to double with a
maximum or pass.

1N-2N-(bid)-
D = 16--17 hcp

** Responses to 2NT and 3NT

The same Stayman and Jacoby-transfer machinery is used one level higher for 2NT,
and two levels higher for 3NT. Opposite 2NT, 4+ hcp is enough for game: 3NT is
to play (4--10), 4NT is quantitative (11--12, NOTES.md "Notrump lane" #N2) and
6NT is to play (13+); 4C (Gerber) is not written here since no range is left
for it. A hand with 0--3 hcp passes.

